      "a": 0,
      "h": "Remember that successive discounts of 20% and 10% equal a net discount of 28%, NOT 30%.",
      "e": "Cost Price (CP) = Rs. 240. Marked Price (MP) = 240 * 1.50 = Rs. 360. Equivalent discount = 20 + 10 - (20*10)/100 = 28%. Selling Price (SP) = MP * (1 - 0.28) = 360 * 0.72 = Rs. 259. Net Profit = 259 - 240 = Rs. 19. Profit % = (19 / 240) * 100 = 7.9%.",
      "step": "Step 1: MP = CP * (1 + 0.50) = Rs. 360.\nStep 2: Net Discount = d1 + d2 - (d1 * d2)/100 = 20 + 10 - 2 = 28%.\nStep 3: SP = MP * (1 - 0.28) = Rs. 259.\nStep 4: Profit % = (SP - CP)/CP * 100 = 7.9%.",
      "tech": "Successive discount equivalence shortcut.",
      "formula": "D_{\\text{eq}} = d_1 + d_2 - \\frac{d_1 d_2}{100}",
