      "topic_id": "quant_partner",
      "topic": "Partnership",
      "difficulty": "Hard",
      "q": "[Partnership Advanced #4] From a group of 13 candidates representing different departments, in how many distinct ways can a committee of 2 delegates be selected without regard to rank or ordering?",
      "o": [
        "78",
        "88",
        "73",
        "156"
      ],
      "a": 0,
      "h": "Use combination formula nCr = n! / (r! * (n - r)!).",
      "e": "Since order of selection does not matter, the number of ways is 13C2 = (13 * 12) / (2 * 1) = 78.",
      "step": "Step 1: Formula nCr = n! / [r! (n-r)!].\nStep 2: Here n = 13, r = 2.\nStep 3: 13C2 = (13 * 12) / 2 = 78.",
      "tech": "Subset combination principle.",
      "formula": "\\binom{n}{2} = \\frac{n(n - 1)}{2}",
      "code": ""
