      "topic_id": "quant_si",
      "topic": "Simple Interest",
      "difficulty": "Hard",
      "q": "[Simple Interest Advanced #5] Worker A can complete a project in 20 days, while Worker B alone requires 30 days. If they collaborate together for the first 2 days and then Worker A leaves, how many days will Worker B take alone to finish the remaining work?",
      "o": [
        "25 days",
        "28 days",
        "23 days",
        "30 days"
      ],
      "a": 0,
      "h": "Calculate the fraction of work completed in the initial 2 days, then divide remaining work by B's daily rate.",
      "e": "A's daily rate is 1/20 and B's is 1/30. Together their combined rate is 1/20 + 1/30 = 5/(60). In 2 days they finish 2 * 5/(60) = 5/(30) of the total work. The remaining work is 1 - 5/(30) = (30-5)/(30). B alone finishes this in (Remaining Work) * 30 = 25 days.",
      "step": "Step 1: Daily rate of A = 1/20; Daily rate of B = 1/30.\nStep 2: Combined 2-day work = 2 * (1/20 + 1/30) = 5/30.\nStep 3: Remaining work = 1 - 5/30 = (30-5)/30.\nStep 4: Time for B = Remaining Work / (1/30) = 25 days.",
      "tech": "Unitary work rate method.",
      "formula": "T_{\\text{rem}} = \\frac{1 - W_{\\text{done}}}{\\text{Rate}_B}",
      "code": ""
