      "topic": "Work and Wages",
      "difficulty": "Hard",
      "q": "[Work and Wages Advanced #3] In what ratio must tea worth Rs. 21 per kg be mixed with tea worth Rs. 36 per kg so that the resulting mixture is worth Rs. 27 per kg?",
      "o": [
        "3 : 2",
        "2 : 3",
        "4 : 2",
        "3 : 3"
      ],
      "a": 0,
      "h": "Apply rule of alligation: Cheaper quantity / Dearer quantity = (Dearer price - Mean price) / (Mean price - Cheaper price).",
      "e": "By Rule of Alligation:\n(Quantity of Cheaper) / (Quantity of Dearer) = (36 - 27) / (27 - 21) = 9 / 6 = 3 : 2.",
      "step": "Step 1: Identify Cheaper price C = 21, Dearer price D = 36, Mean price M = 27.\nStep 2: D - M = 36 - 27 = 9.\nStep 3: M - C = 27 - 21 = 6.\nStep 4: Required ratio = 9 : 6 = 3 : 2.",
      "tech": "Rule of Alligation.",
      "formula": "\\frac{Q_{\\text{cheaper}}}{Q_{\\text{dearer}}} = \\frac{D - M}{M - C}",
      "code": ""
