      "h": "When traveling in opposite directions, relative speed is the sum of both speeds. Convert km/h to m/s by multiplying by 5/18.",
      "e": "Total distance to clear = length_1 + length_2 = 70 + 105 = 175 m. Since they travel in opposite directions, relative speed = 60 + 40 = 100 km/h = 100 * (5/18) = 27.778 m/s. Time = Distance / Speed = 175 / 27.778 = 6.3 seconds.",
      "step": "Step 1: Total crossing distance = 70 + 105 = 175 m.\nStep 2: Relative speed = 60 + 40 = 100 km/h.\nStep 3: Convert to m/s: 100 * (5/18) = 27.78 m/s.\nStep 4: Time = 175 / 27.78 = 6.3 s.",
      "tech": "Relative speed opposite direction formulation.",
      "formula": "T = \\frac{L_1 + L_2}{(S_1 + S_2) \\times \\frac{5}{18}}",
