      "difficulty": "Hard",
      "q": "Calculate the geometric spatial dimension:\nTrigonometric Bilateral Observation #6: Two monitoring vehicles are positioned on opposite sides of a transmission tower of height 28 meters. The observed angles of elevation to the top of the tower are 30 degrees and 45 degrees respectively. Taking sqrt(3) = 1.732, what is the total ground distance separating the two vehicles?",
      "o": [
        "91.0 m",
        "64.3 m",
        "76.5 m",
        "107.1 m"
      ],
      "a": 2,
      "h": "Sum the cotangent projections from both sides of the tower.",
      "e": "Distance from vehicle 1 = 28 / tan(30 deg) = 28 * sqrt(3) = 48.5 m. Distance from vehicle 2 = 28 / tan(45 deg) = 28 m. Total separation = 28*(1.732 + 1) = 76.5 m.",
      "step": "Step 1: Subdivide base into two right triangles.\nStep 2: Base 1 = h * cot(30 deg) = 28 * 1.732. Base 2 = h * cot(45 deg) = 28.\nStep 3: Sum base segments: 28*(2.732) = 76.5 m.",
      "tech": "Bilateral trigonometric elevation resolution.",
      "formula": "D = h(\\cot 30^\\circ + \\cot 45^\\circ)",
      "code": ""
