      "topic": "Height and Distance",
      "difficulty": "Easy",
      "q": "Compute the kinematics motion parameter:\nAn autonomous marine research vessel travels at 24 km/h in calm waters. A tidal ocean current flows steadily at 6 km/h. If the vessel navigates 1080 km downstream and then returns upstream to its starting dock, what is the total round-trip journey time?",
      "o": [
        "96 hours",
        "100 hours",
        "93 hours",
        "104 hours"
      ],
      "a": 0,
      "h": "Downstream adds stream speed; upstream subtracts it.",
      "e": "Downstream speed = 24 + 6 = 30 km/h. Time downstream = 1080/30 = 36 hrs. Upstream speed = 24 - 6 = 18 km/h. Time upstream = 1080/18 = 60 hrs. Total time = 96 hrs.",
      "step": "Step 1: Effective downstream velocity: v_d = 24 + 6 = 30 km/h.\nStep 2: Effective upstream velocity: v_u = 24 - 6 = 18 km/h.\nStep 3: Total duration: T = 1080/30 + 1080/18 = 96 hours.",
      "tech": "Relative fluid kinematics vector summation.",
      "formula": "T_{\\text{total}} = \\frac{D}{v + u} + \\frac{D}{v - u}",
      "code": ""
