      "topic": "Combination",
      "difficulty": "Easy",
      "q": "Calculate the exact combinatorial or probabilistic value:\nCombinatorics Problem #3: A card is drawn at random from a standard 52-card deck. What is the probability of drawing either a King or a Heart?",
      "o": [
        "4/13",
        "17/52",
        "1/4",
        "9/26"
      ],
      "a": 0,
      "h": "Identify whether order matters and apply multiplication rule.",
      "e": "P(King or Heart) = P(King) + P(Heart) - P(King of Hearts) = 4/52 + 13/52 - 1/52 = 16/52 = 4/13.",
      "step": "Step 1: P(King) = 4/52, P(Heart) = 13/52.\nStep 2: Intersection = 1/52.\nStep 3: Total = (4 + 13 - 1)/52 = 16/52 = 4/13.",
      "tech": "Classical counting principles and probability distributions.",
      "formula": "P(A \\cup B) = P(A) + P(B) - P(A \\cap B)",
      "code": ""
