      "q": "[Divisibility Rules Basic #1] A quantity increases by 20% to reach 43. What was the original value?",
      "o": [
        "36",
        "42",
        "30",
        "48"
      ],
      "a": 0,
      "h": "Divide the increased total by 1.20.",
      "e": "Original value = 43 / 1.20 = 36.",
      "step": "Step 1: New value = Original * (1 + 0.20) = 1.2 * Original.\nStep 2: Original = 43 / 1.2.\nStep 3: Original = 36.",
      "tech": "Base percentage scaling.",
      "formula": "X_0 = \\frac{X_{\\text{new}}}{1 + r}",
      "code": ""
