      "e": "Distance from vehicle 1 = 28 / tan(30 deg) = 28 * sqrt(3) = 48.5 m. Distance from vehicle 2 = 28 / tan(45 deg) = 28 m. Total separation = 28*(1.732 + 1) = 76.5 m.",
      "step": "Step 1: Subdivide base into two right triangles.\nStep 2: Base 1 = h * cot(30 deg) = 28 * 1.732. Base 2 = h * cot(45 deg) = 28.\nStep 3: Sum base segments: 28*(2.732) = 76.5 m.",
      "tech": "Bilateral trigonometric elevation resolution.",
      "formula": "D = h(\\cot 30^\\circ + \\cot 45^\\circ)",
      "code": ""
